{
 "version": 1,
 "about": "G38 (operator, 2026-11-08): pooling skips the chat template's FIXED PREFIX, pinned for BOTH repos. The prefix is the common prefix of the SERVED ids of two content-free renders - [{role: user, content: x}] and [{role: user, content: y}], add_generation_prompt false, each tokenized by the start-of-text rule (prompt_encoding.rendered_chat_ids) - so it holds the start token, the template's preamble and the first user header, never content; it is empty when the template refuses either render or the two renders are identical. P for a row is the length of the row's served ids' common prefix with it (a row with its own system prompt skips only what it shares, G38-3), measured against the cached prefix and re-measured once against a freshly rendered one when the row does not begin with all of it (a date-stamped preamble). With aggregation.skip_template_prefix true, positions [0, P) are left out of the windows that contain them, `all`, `prompt` and `last_user` (whose span becomes [max(start, P), end)); `response` is unchanged. miWorkbench computes it in probe_monitor_render (template_prefix_ids, RenderedExample.scored_mask) and miServer in probe_turns (template_prefix_ids, template_prefix_length) and probe_scope.scored_mask; each repo runs its own code over these cases and asserts P and every window's mask, and asserts this file is byte-identical to the other repo's copy. Masks are strings over the served ids, '1' = scored. A row whose role mask is unreliable scores no last_user window.",
 "structural": {
  "about": "Tokenizer-free: each repo builds a WordLevel tokenizer over `vocab` with a WhitespaceSplit pre-tokenizer, unk_token [UNK], bos_token <s> and - when tokenizer_adds_bos - a TemplateProcessing post-processor single='<s> $A'. The chat template is templates[case.template]. A case may carry its own `vocab`. A case carrying `stale_cached_prefix` (token strings) has that prefix PLANTED in the repo's prefix cache before the row is measured - the state a date-stamped (strftime_now) preamble leaves after midnight, made deterministic. These ALWAYS run.",
  "vocab": [
   "<s>",
   "<|user|>",
   "<|assistant|>",
   "<|system|>",
   "<|end|>",
   "cutting",
   "knowledge",
   "date",
   "be",
   "brief",
   "a",
   "b",
   "x",
   "y",
   "first",
   "question",
   "an",
   "answer",
   "virus",
   "spreads",
   "fast",
   "[UNK]"
  ],
  "templates": {
   "preamble": "<s> {% if messages[0]['role'] != 'system' %}<|system|> cutting knowledge date <|end|> {% endif %}{% for m in messages %}<|{{ m['role'] }}|> {{ m['content'] }} <|end|> {% endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}<|assistant|> {% endif %}",
   "bos": "<s> {% for m in messages %}<|{{ m['role'] }}|> {{ m['content'] }} <|end|> {% endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}<|assistant|> {% endif %}",
   "no_bos": "{% for m in messages %}<|{{ m['role'] }}|> {{ m['content'] }} <|end|> {% endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}<|assistant|> {% endif %}",
   "refuses_a_lone_user_turn": "<s> {% if messages[0]['role'] != 'system' %}{{ raise_exception('a system prompt is required') }}{% endif %}{% for m in messages %}<|{{ m['role'] }}|> {{ m['content'] }} <|end|> {% endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}<|assistant|> {% endif %}"
  },
